<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31955" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεχειρία</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχω, χείρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cessation of hostilities, armistice, truce,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.96.22
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.117
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγειν, ἔχειν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.2.16
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γίγνεταί τισι πρὸς ἀλλήλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.58
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπειπεῖν τὴν ἐ.</span>
			denounce the <i>truce,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.32
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ὀλυμπιακὴ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					533
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεχηπία</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1126.49
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				559.32
			</span></i> (Megalop., found at <i><span class="en">
				Magn.
			</span></i> Mae.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			generally, <i>rest from work, holiday,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				1.1.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4224.17
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.153c
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>leisure, opportunity,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ διαμαρτάνειν, εἰς τὸ ἁμαρτάνειν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.430
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.76
			</span></i> : c. inf., ib. <i><span class="en">
				444
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				908
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέχοντα τὴν ἐκεχειρίαν</span> is a
			pun —'alleging the <i>truce',</i> and 'presenting the
				<i>hand-for-holding'</i> (as a beggar does). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>licence, leave,</i> to do a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. διδόναι τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.542
				</span></i>
			 ; coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄδεια,</span> ib.
				<i><span class="en">
				447
			</span></i>, al. ; <i>time of licence,</i> ib. <i><span class="en">
				529
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>self-restraint, abstinence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὰς κλοπάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					15.1.53
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
